Falsifies `kernel::syscall::proofs::every_page_between_the_checked_ends_is_itself_a_user_page`.

The defect is the widening the harness's doc names as the thing that would break it silently: the
low half stops being a contiguous prefix of the address space. `Half::Low` here also admits the
band at `top == 2`, as a second user island. Both ends of a run can then sit in user bands while
the pages between them (band 1) are not user pages, and the map loop, which checks only the two
ends, walks straight through them. The patch is in `crates/paging`, the code the harness's guard
model calls, so the harness is untouched.

Expected to fail: the harness's last assertion, `is_user_page_va(page_va)` ("every page the map loop touches is an
aligned user-half page"), at the middle page `k` the solver picks.

